Dear [redacted], 

This is to acknowledge receipt of your Access to Information Act (Act) request received on April 13, 2026, for:

Records (e-mails, briefing notes, risk assessment, and formal assessment summaries) held by ADM(Materiel) related to the evaluation of the Canadian Patrol Submarine Project (CPSP), from January 1, 2024 to April 11, 2026 including:

1)     Hanwha Ocean CPSP submission and associated Industrial and Technological Benefits (ITB) obligations

2)     Canadian academic or industry partnerships identified in Hanwha’s ITB proposal

3)     Compliance assessments regarding applicable Canadian legal and policy requirements related to supply chains and labour practices

4)     Gender Based Analysis (GBA+), Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) assessments conducted in relation to entities proposed as ITB partners

5)     Responses to external or civil society input concerning governance, partnerships, or related concerns tied to the Hanwha CPSP bid

6)     Comparative evaluation records assessing Hanwha Ocean vs. TKMS (Germany) on governance, compliance, or risk factors

7)     Korean university engineering ecosystem capacity for long-term technology transfer and sustainment obligations

8)     Records discussing Article 92-6 of the Republic of Korea Military Criminal Act in relation to procurement, human rights considerations, or potential implications for CPSP evaluation or long-term sustainment.

